# `node_modules` here is a SYMLINK to ../personal-website/node_modules.
# Git treats a symlink as a file, and a pattern with a trailing slash matches
# directories only — so `node_modules/` alone would NOT ignore it and the link
# would get committed. Both forms are listed deliberately.
node_modules
node_modules/

.next/
out/
.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Supabase credentials. `.env.local.example` is the committed template and is
# explicitly re-included; everything holding a real value stays out.
.env
.env.local
.env*.local
!.env.local.example

# Local, machine-specific Claude Code permissions.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Generated by `npm run sql:bundle` — the numbered migrations are the source.
supabase/migrations/APPLY_ALL.generated.sql
supabase/migrations/RUN_ME.generated.sql

# The brand kit as delivered. 85MB, most of it the 74MB `ESE Magic Hour.pdf` and
# PNG exports that the committed `.ai` files supersede. The build inputs are
# extracted into `ref_docs/brand/`, and that directory's README transcribes what
# the walkthrough says, so nothing the site depends on lives only in the archive.
# Drive exports. The first rule only matched the ESE-prefixed zip, so a
# differently-named export slipped into a commit; this covers both shapes.
ESE*-*-001.zip
drive-download-*.zip

# Added by `vercel link`. `.env*` is broader than the block above and, being
# later in the file, overrides the `!.env.local.example` negation there — git
# applies the LAST matching pattern. The negation is therefore repeated below,
# after it, or the committed template becomes invisible in a fresh clone.
.vercel
.env*
!.env.local.example

# The 430MB of master footage supplied for the section backdrops. This is the
# SOURCE folder, not an asset folder — nothing here is served.
# `scripts/build-section-videos.mjs` transcodes it into `public/video/`, and it is
# `public/video/` that ships (17MB, committed). Keeping the masters out of git is
# deliberate: they are an order of magnitude larger than the entire rest of the
# repository and would be carried in every clone forever.
# Anyone re-running the build script needs this folder restored from wherever the
# footage was originally licensed.
videos/
